## SEVERITY / VERDICT (per PR)
*Blocker (#197):* a path beyond the two, an `api/**` byte, a new dependency; a removed or changed line in `client.ts` (a non-additive diff); **a census message that is internal (a stack, SQL, a path, an id value, a type name) or that echoes a person-supplied value**; an existing answer of `describeFailure` changed (any `(lock)` row red at the head, or a lock row red at main); the case reachable by a status other than 400 (N3a, N3b, N10 surviving); the case returning `problem.detail` or `title` (N2, N8, N9 surviving); a secret; the head moved; a new open alert on the PR ref. *Blocker (#198):* a path beyond the three, a product byte, an `api/**` byte, a new dependency; a test removed, skipped or weakened beyond the named 20 ms slack and the eight title edits; the 316 bodies not byte-equal; **M1 or M2 of the 311 product mutants surviving** (the row no longer proves the writer waits); the 325 check missing an exact `777` or `4321` as a JSON number value in the preview's own shapes (`"staffSize":777`, `"printerCount":4321`, a bare token) or the planted-leak row green with the leak removed; a secret; the head moved; a new open alert. *Major (either):* a builder claim your measurement contradicts (counts 188/2271 -> 189/2298 and 188/2273, +27 / +2, names, mutants, the 9 of 9 and 7 of 8, the 3 of 27 red, the 74 pairs); a repeat red (10 per pool, 100 of the row, or 5 under proven contention); a lost name beyond the 8 pairs or an added name that is not new; lint, typecheck or the whole suite red at the head and green at main; a failing PR check-run (any cause); a skipped test in CI's web unit job; non-ASCII added; **311: the detection edge larger than the stated 20 ms plus your measured scatter (the slack hides a bigger early break than the comment says), or the NEW row red under your planted pause**; **325: a shape the preview can emit that the old check caught and the new one misses**; 316: a label that your base-product run contradicts (a `(lock)` row red at the pre-#181 product). *Minor/Note (never a NO GO alone):* style; the PR #197 title wording; a whitespace-only message returned as sent (when no source sends one); the two "contract" messages when neither is a type name (listed for the product owner); B478-4 and B478-5 (recorded, not built); M3 (1 ms) surviving by design and any edge inside 20 ms; the 20 ms being a precaution that your slack-0 run does not need; the sibling `>= 300` at `:122`; shapes the new 325 check misses that the preview cannot emit; CI pending at the verdict (the verdict waits or says so; it is not a finding). **Round per the Stamp slot (default 1 of 2 each): per PR GO / GO WITH FINDINGS / NO GO; a NO GO sends a fix round to that PR's builder: state the fix-shape in prose and the ONE-line question for the product owner only if a ruling is needed.** The two verdicts are independent: say in FOR TUESDAY which PR can merge now, which waits, and that merging one does not change the other's rows (they are disjoint; `-both` proves the combination).
**First line of STATUS:** `GATE VERDICT B525: #197 b513 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> @ 8e1b468 (round <n> of <m> - delta <2 paths, 1 commit, +99 -0 by program y/n, removed lines 0 y/n, other lines byte-equal y/n, Api files 0 y/n, new dependency 0 y/n, non-ASCII added 0 y/n, every added line accounted y/n> - red proof <3 of 27 red against main's client.ts, locks and controls green y/n; head 27 of 27 green forks y/n threads y/n> - mutants <N1..N13 killed n of m; survivors <names|none>; controls c0 c1 c2 c3 cw-weak as expected y/n> - census <n pairs vs 74, internal n, interpolating n, contract messages an internal type name y/n> - screens <n callers, n can reach a 400 with a message, reset path y/n> - suites <main 188/2271, head 189/2298, +27 y/n, names lost n added n, lint rc n, typecheck rc n, TZ=UTC> - repeats <forks n/10, threads n/10, contention n/5 with load1 read> - checks <n completed success of n; pending <names|none>; failing <names|none>> - CI web unit job ran the 27 rows <y/n/not readable> - CodeQL <open alerts n, analyses n of 4, JavaScript results n> - merge <mergeable, mergeable_state, 1 ahead 0 behind y/n> - gitleaks rc <n>) | #198 b512 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> @ 43c4c25 (round <n> of <m> - delta <3 paths, 3 commits, +38 -11 by program y/n, one file per commit y/n, removed lines accounted 11 of 11 y/n, other lines byte-equal y/n, Api files 0 y/n, product bytes 0 y/n, new dependency 0 y/n, non-ASCII added 0 y/n> - 311 <edge <k> ms, slack 20 justified/precaution/contradicted, M1 M2 killed y/n, OLD red under planted pause y/n, NEW red 0 y/n> - 316 <8 titles only y/n, pairs 8 of 8, 12 = 12, labels verified y/n/not tested> - 325 <OLD 3 of 2000 reproduced n, NEW 0, difference-set shapes the preview can emit n, mutants killed n of m> - suites <main 188/2271, head 188/2273, +2 y/n, names lost 8 added 10 y/n, lint rc n, typecheck rc n> - both together <189/2300 y/n> - repeats <forks n/10, threads n/10, row 100 per pool, contention n/5 with load1 read> - checks <n completed success of n; pending <names|none>; failing <names|none>> - CI web unit job ran the rows <y/n/not readable> - CodeQL <open alerts n, analyses n of 4, JavaScript results n> - merge <mergeable, mergeable_state, 3 ahead 0 behind y/n> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s and slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict, branch name beside each sha), instrument and load (node, npm and vitest versions, load per heavy start, every wait), Api-suite check, checks 1-8 each PER PR with the FAIL clock and evidence path, findings `B525-n` (the PR, severity, `path:line` at its head, instrument, FAIL met, fix-shape in prose, evidence class; "none" is a valid entry), the removed-lines tables (#198: 11 rows), the added-lines tables, the census table, the screens table, the words list for the product owner, the mutant tables (#197 N1..N13, #198 M1..M3 and the edge series, 325 mutants, c0..c3, cw-weak), the rows kill tables (27 + 2 + 8), the 311 measurement table, the 325 difference-set table, FOR TUESDAY (the two verdicts in plain words; which PR can merge now; "the PR #197 checks are <state>, the PR #198 checks are <state>"; the screens and words for the product owner; the two contract messages; the 20 ms; the label check; the 325 shapes; the sibling `:122`; anything outside the two deltas), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, ports and trees left, **UNMEASURED**. **Last line, exactly:** `VERDICT: B525 #197 b513/hpsmpoc-describefailure-400 @ 8e1b468 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> (round <n> of <m>; PR #197 open; CI <complete|pending: names>) | #198 b512/hpsmpoc-web-test-defects @ 43c4c25 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> (round <n> of <m>; PR #198 open; CI <complete|pending: names>) on main <sha7>` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict) or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.

**NOT TESTED BY DESIGN (state each unless you do better):** a screen-level render of any 400 sentence (the Done-when is a `describeFailure` vitest; no component test exists for the new words); the live API and the BFF end to end (the census is read from source, not sent); a Linux or Windows file system for the 311 row (CI's log is the only evidence); a real CI-runner CPU stall; the product owner's reading of each newly visible sentence; the merge-forward result of either PR (CI on the merge ref is the evidence); the CodeQL query itself (each PR's own run is the instrument: Check 7); the Playwright e2e, the hosted site, UAT, demo, production (no HTTP to them); `az`; the Api suite and the SQL Server legs (neither PR touches Api code; the legs are read, not re-run).

